{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3440","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3440","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3440\",\"parent_revision\":\"016924e9804e3ec5714dabecd5a1f2f408f1e6c63e32fc869f6968bae7c1d2c6\",\"root_revision\":\"016924e9804e3ec5714dabecd5a1f2f408f1e6c63e32fc869f6968bae7c1d2c6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA repo-wide sweep of every plugin's runtime files found 200 references that resolve only in this repository. python-engineering carries 36.\\n\\nAn escape is a path, markdown link, or cross-plugin mention in a plugin's runtime files (skills/ and agents/) that points outside the plugin that ships it. An installed consumer does not have this repository, so the reference resolves for the author alone and silently fails for everyone else.\\n\\nREPRODUCTION\\n\\n    uv run plugins/plugin-creator/skills/lint/scripts/audit_runtime_escapes.py \\\\\\n        --plugin-dir plugins/python-engineering\\n\\nThe full report for all plugins, including this plugin's per-line findings, is regenerated with --all.\\n\\nIMPACT\\n\\nEach escape is an instruction an agent cannot follow once the plugin is installed anywhere but here. The failure is silent: the agent reads a path, finds nothing, and continues without the guidance the reference was meant to supply.\\n\\nSWEEP CONTEXT\\n\\n200 escapes across 12 plugins; 17 of 29 plugins are already clean. Counts: the-rewrite-room 40, plugin-creator 38, python-engineering 36, development-harness 32, python3-development 31, agentskill-kaizen 7, scientific-method 7, fastmcp-creator 3, orchestrator-discipline 3, agent-orchestration 1, perl-development 1, summarizer 1.\\n\\nTwo known limits of the scanner apply to this count. It covers skills/ and agents/ only, so commands/, plugin-root CLAUDE.md, plugin-root references/ and docs/ are unscanned and real escapes live there \u2014 the true number is higher. Its report header is also hardcoded to name development-harness regardless of which plugin was scanned. Both are tracked separately.\\n\\nUser-provided context: the rule these violate is documented at plugins/plugin-creator/docs/runtime-environment.md, which covers the two audiences, the environment split, and the three-part check. Remediation is usually one of: move the target inside the plugin, replace a repo path with a URL, or delete a reference that was design-time content in a runtime file.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Repo-wide runtime escape sweep, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"a390cf11b8ac82fe91af92a093cd0f69ce10ae61a9c3cb5367e224a03cec77b8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABTSAw6A\"}"}